    "title": "Karol G Talks Headlining Coachella, Teases Sunday Night Set",
    "text": "Karol G is teasing her upcoming closing set at 2026 Coachella Music Festival! The 35-year-old Grammy-winning Colombian singer will be performing at the annual event on Sunday night (April 12) as the final headlining act on the Coachella stage, aka the main stage. Keep reading to find out more… “Right now I’m just a rollercoaster of feelings and emotions and even with the preparation and the rehearsal and the studying, all this process for this show had opened my mind in so many different way, so I, every day, just see something different,” she shared on Call Her Daddy. “I feel super blessed, of course. I feel super responsible of a lot of things. I feel super proud at the same time. I feel super nervous. I don’t know if you know, but I finished the tour, Mañana Será Bonito Tour, in July 2024 and since that July, I haven’t been on stage like no, with a show of mine. Bad Bunny was in Medellín, so I sang with him a song that we have together, but not me on stage performing like a full show and this is crazy ’cause I love my fans [laughs].” She also shared that she’s going to “present” her latest album, Tropicoqueta, at the festival, admitting she’s more than nervous. “I’m like, I need to be on stage. I love stage,” Karol says. “For me, being on the studio, doing music and being on stage, like it’s my happiest place to be.” The singer even dished on representing her community with this opportunity. “This is huge. I think to have a purpose is the most important thing. Even when we started talking about the creative details of the show, I was like, ‘Let’s start from the message,’ ’cause I love shows, but I love to be on shows that they have a meaning, they have a reason, they have something to stand for, and this is my opportunity to stand for my community,” she said. “You know, as an artist and being there, I’ve all the times feel that we can have a voice, but sometimes it’s not enough. But to be on that specific stage is to have a big voice. This opportunity to have a big voice for them, so yeah. I’m happy they’re speaking a little loud.” If you missed it, Karol G is currently scheduled to hit the stage at Coachella at 9:55pm PT on Sunday (April 12). See the full list of set times here! She also recently opened up about her relationship status and the pressure to have kids.",
